# nginx – Beispiel für Nexis (Document Root = Projektroot)

Siehe ADR 006 und [06 Sicherheit](../06-sicherheit-und-betrieb.md#611-document-root-im-projektordner). Pfade anpassen.

```nginx
server {
    listen 443 ssl http2;
    server_name example.com;
    root /var/www/nexis;
    index index.php;

    # ssl_certificate …;
    # ssl_certificate_key …;

    # Statische Assets direkt
    location ^~ /assets/ {
        try_files $uri =404;
        access_log off;
        expires 7d;
    }

    # Geschützte Pfade
    location ~* ^/(\.env|composer\.(json|lock)|phpunit\.xml) {
        deny all;
        return 403;
    }
    location ~* ^/(src|vendor|config|storage|database|tests|docs|bin|plugins|resources)/ {
        deny all;
        return 403;
    }
    location ~* ^/themes/.+\.(twig|json|md)$ {
        deny all;
        return 403;
    }
    location ~ /\. {
        deny all;
        return 403;
    }

    location / {
        try_files $uri $uri/ /index.php?$query_string;
    }

    location ~ \.php$ {
        include fastcgi_params;
        fastcgi_param SCRIPT_FILENAME $document_root$fastcgi_script_name;
        fastcgi_param HTTPS on;
        fastcgi_pass unix:/run/php/php8.4-fpm.sock;
    }
}

server {
    listen 80;
    server_name example.com;
    return 301 https://$host$request_uri;
}
```

Hinter einem weiteren Reverse Proxy in `.env` die Proxy-IP setzen:

```env
TRUSTED_PROXIES=10.0.0.1
APP_URL=https://example.com
```
